    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 22nd with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), whose aggressive presence on the basepaths is amplified by a favorable matchup against Kodai Senga. Given our focus on the scarcest category of stolen bases, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier start; despite a minor efficiency dip due to Senga\u2019s ability to control the run game, his elite speed profile and leadoff role provide the highest projected contribution today. Close behind in output is **Christian Yelich** (74.33), who benefits from a significant platoon advantage against Brady Singer and favorable wind conditions that could turn fly balls into scoring opportunities, alongside **Caleb Durbin** (71.72), who draws a lucrative matchup against the struggling Ryan Feltner.\n\nOur roster configuration highlights several calculated risks, most notably with **Yordan Alvarez** (61.66), who remains a locked-in starter despite a difficult matchup against the elite arm of Dylan Cease. While his raw base projection is high, his score is suppressed by Cease's 3.15 xERA, yet his xwOBA profile remains too potent to bench. Conversely, the most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Pedro Ramirez** (52.85). He was the primary candidate for a utility spot but ultimately stayed on the bench behind more favorable platoon matchups, as the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency of **Nelson Velazquez** (56.94) and **Dillon Dingler** (48.54).\n\nManagers should maintain vigilance regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Gary Sanchez** and **Kazuma Okamoto**, as their final batting order positions are critical to meeting our efficiency thresholds. **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a particularly challenging task today against Hunter Brown (3.31 xERA); his sub-45 score puts him on the absolute edge of our starting requirements. While the roster is currently set to maximize category coverage\u2014specifically focusing on speed and OBP\u2014any late lineup shifts dropping **Trea Turner** or **Kyle Schwarber** from their projected spots would trigger an immediate re-evaluation of the bench depth, potentially bringing **Chase Meidroth** or **Carson Benge** into the fold if we need to preserve games played.",
